# GBNF grammar for the local LLM extractor (Cursor-Mileage-Plan §6.2).
#
# Constrains decoding so the model's output CANNOT escape this schema — no
# retry-on-parse-failure needed, the decoder physically cannot emit anything
# else. Mirrors `RawChartRow` exactly (program, region_a<-from, region_b<-to,
# cabin, miles, roundtrip), so a valid parse drops straight into
# `_build_charts()` with no new parsing surface (see local_extractor.py).
#
# This file is the canonical schema definition for BOTH serving paths:
#   - llama.cpp / llama-cpp-python: pass this file's contents directly as the
#     `grammar` argument (LlamaGrammar.from_string / --grammar-file).
#   - Ollama: as of writing, Ollama's HTTP API takes a JSON Schema via its
#     `format` field rather than a raw .gbnf string, so local_extractor.py's
#     OllamaExtractor mirrors this SAME schema as a JSON Schema dict inline
#     rather than loading this file at runtime. Keep the two in sync if this
#     file changes. If/when Ollama accepts GBNF directly, this file becomes
#     the single source of truth for both backends — that's the point of
#     keeping it checked in now rather than only inlining the JSON Schema.
#
# `cabin` is constrained to the four canonical values domain/models.py and
# parse.py's `_CABINS` already accept — an out-of-vocabulary cabin is a schema
# violation, not a row the resolver would understand anyway.
#
# NOTE: `from`/`to` are free-text region/city/country strings as they appear
# in the source prose (e.g. "Turkey", "North America", "LAX") — NOT
# constrained to an enum here, because the source text's own vocabulary can't
# be predicted ahead of time. They are canonicalized after generation via the
# SAME `regions.canonicalize_region()` every deterministic parser already
# uses (see local_extractor.py); a region that doesn't canonicalize is
# dropped, never guessed — identical contract to every other intake.

root    ::= "[" ws (row ("," ws row)*)? ws "]"

row     ::= "{" ws
            "\"program\"" ws ":" ws str "," ws
            "\"from\"" ws ":" ws str "," ws
            "\"to\"" ws ":" ws str "," ws
            "\"cabin\"" ws ":" ws cabin "," ws
            "\"miles\"" ws ":" ws int "," ws
            "\"roundtrip\"" ws ":" ws bool ws
            "}"

cabin   ::= "\"economy\"" | "\"premium_economy\"" | "\"business\"" | "\"first\""
bool    ::= "true" | "false"
int     ::= [0-9]{1,7}
str     ::= "\"" char* "\""
char    ::= [^"\\] | "\\" escape
escape  ::= ["\\/bfnrt] | "u" hex hex hex hex
hex     ::= [0-9a-fA-F]
ws      ::= [ \t\n\r]*
